From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 11:37:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] plugins: qemu_plugin_read_memory_vaddr_fault, page-in reads
 at a hook

Add a plugin API that reads guest virtual memory and, on a miss, raises the
architectural fault a load at the instrumented instruction would take, so
the guest pages the address in and re-runs the callback at the same PC.

- RW_REGS_PC callbacks are entered through a trampoline that records the
  host return address into the TB (cpu->neg.plugin_cb_ra), so the API can
  unwind to the instruction start with cpu_restore_state semantics.
- TCGCPUOps.user_mmu_index (x86, arm, mips) to translate as an
  unprivileged access (LDTR / CPL3), needed under SMAP/PAN.
- Never reads non-RAM (MMIO) pages.
---
